    <p>A <strong>word equation</strong> uses the names of substances to show a chemical reaction. The starting substances are the <strong>reactants</strong> (on the left); the new substances are the <strong>products</strong> (on the right). A plus sign means “and” or “reacts with”, and the arrow means “forms”.</p>
